# OPTIONAL — NOT APPLIED. For David's review before any public-exposure change on the VPS.
#
# The watch party already works through the existing sharplab.djiang.xyz site with NO Caddy change:
#   page   https://sharplab.djiang.xyz/wall.html     (the site's catch-all file_server, web/static/wall.html)
#   HLS    /api/v1/wall/hls/*                        (handle /api/* → localhost:8000; session-checked in web/wall.py)
#   socket /ws/wall                                  (handle /ws/* → localhost:8000; session-checked at the handshake)
# The homelab wall service (100.67.232.59:7795) is only reached by sharplab-web over Tailscale with WALL_API_TOKEN;
# nothing here proxies to it, and its control API (/presets, /i/*) is never routed publicly.
#
# What this adds, if wanted: a pretty /wall URL. Paste inside the `sharplab.djiang.xyz { … }` block, next to the
# other page rewrites (above the catch-all `root * /opt/sharplab/web/static` / `file_server`), then
# `caddy validate --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile && systemctl reload caddy`.

    @wallPage path /wall /wall/
    handle @wallPage {
        rewrite * /wall.html
        root * /opt/sharplab/web/static
        file_server
    }

# Not recommended, listed for completeness: serving HLS straight from the homelab with Caddy forward_auth (saves the
# app proxying ~4.5 Mb/s per distinct segment, which the app caches, so N viewers ≈ one upstream fetch anyway):
#
#    handle_path /wall/hls/* {
#        forward_auth localhost:8000 {
#            uri /api/v1/wall/me          # 200 with a session, 401 without
#        }
#        rewrite * /hls/discord{path}
#        reverse_proxy 100.67.232.59:7795 {
#            header_up Authorization "Bearer {env.WALL_API_TOKEN}"
#        }
#    }
